Error: Jet.ValueTypeMismatch: `count` is a U8 for its use on line 12, but this use needs a Float
  --> Tests/UI/number_name_two_uses_conflict.jet:11:16
    |
 11 |     print(half(count))
    |                ^^^^^
  --> Tests/UI/number_name_two_uses_conflict.jet:12:17
    |
 12 |     print(small(count))
    |                 ^^^^^ this use makes `count` a U8
 Why: A changeable number name takes the type of the first use that refuses its default, and one name holds one type
 Fix: Convert the value at one of the two uses, or give each use its own name
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueTypeMismatch
